{{Quote|Be very, very quiet. Evolved Hunter throws a net that stuns the closest troop. If that troop is flying, it'll ground them.}}

The Hunter Evolution is an {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked with 6 Evolution Shards. It spawns a Hunter with identical stats to the original. The Evolved Hunter will throw a net at the closest unit every 5 seconds. The net will freeze the troop in place and render it unable to move or attack, and allow ground units to hit the trapped unit for 3 seconds. He appears as a man who wears a team-colored coonskin cap with purple hair, a golden stripe and a [[Card Evolution]] symbol in the middle, a brown cloth, gloves, belt, pants and boots, an indigo shirt, and team-colored wristlets, is armed with a double-barreled shotgun, wield nets with purple points, and has fuzzy black eyebrows and mustache covering his eyes and mouth respectively. The Hunter's Evolution costs 4 [[Elixir]] and requires 2 cycles to deploy.

== Strategy==
*Combining him with [[Skeletons/Evolution|Evolved Skeletons]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Bats]], [[Goblin Gang]], or [[Minion Horde]] can fully counter a LavaLoon combo, commonly known as the [[Lava Hound]] and [[Balloon]] combo push, for a massive positive Elixir trade.
*If there is only 1 unit against Hunter, then that unit will be stun-locked forever, as the duration and hit speed of the net is the same as the cooldown.
*The Evolved Hunter performs slightly worse against [[Graveyard]] than his [[Hunter|regular counterpart]] due to his net animation. The net itself won't make a difference against the Skeletons, but the net animation makes it so that his attack animation is slightly delayed, allowing for some more Skeleton hits on your [[Crown Tower]].

